{"id": "EUVD-2026-82029", "enisaUuid": "e6f9c664-a89b-3be7-9191-e0180ea44340", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7915: unwind state on add_interface failure\n\nWhen mt76_wcid_alloc() fails, mt7915_add_interface() returned without\nclearing the vif_mask/omac_mask bits it had already set, without removing\nthe firmware dev info added earlier, and without clearing a monitor_vif\npointer to the vif mac80211 is about to free. mac80211 does not call\nremove_interface() for a failed add, so the indices and firmware dev\nentry leaked permanently and testmode could dereference the stale\nmonitor_vif. Add a proper error unwind.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7198d8fcfdd3ebef3dfbb6073267a053b09f6a05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/218fdf0fcb796b8d281dbdd4a6144c5a8fc7fd0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/507eddb8175a67df5086354b92d6a4fd7f6f1f96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71bf9de2ab3fb2c54bedb0b4c9b468d2e1d55280", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2fb6480c52f611338e1b0abe5e6219be1fc9ab75"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f4w3-pjj6-cfwj", "CVE-2026-90368"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04966b5b-c4a7-31f2-acfd-89ba3dc3b567", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "0d8a4a46-e6c8-3c1a-bbcb-c58c791e03c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b619e01380eedf24e8d26a367e94e0ccaeb0c3dd <2fb6480c52f611338e1b0abe5e6219be1fc9ab75"}, {"id": "267414f5-079f-3ca1-97cd-e930e8dbbfaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b619e01380eedf24e8d26a367e94e0ccaeb0c3dd <507eddb8175a67df5086354b92d6a4fd7f6f1f96"}, {"id": "4060e615-e2c9-3057-8c3d-a9f7d610a812", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.19"}, {"id":